# Logging

Human reference: `docs/logging.md`. When adding or changing logs, follow level semantics first, then Dhara conventions below.

## Standard level hierarchy

Severity decreases top → bottom; verbosity increases. **Configured level captures that level and everything more severe** (`logged >= threshold`).

```
FATAL/CRITICAL  — unrecoverable; process must stop
ERROR           — operation failed; app continues
WARN            — unusual but non-blocking; investigate later
INFO            — healthy milestones operators rely on in production
DEBUG           — engineer diagnostics; usually off in production
TRACE           — line-by-line / per-item detail; highest volume
```

| Pick this level when… | Example |
| --------------------- | ------- |
| ERROR | Module/command aborts; user-visible failure | subprocess or handler hard failure |
| WARN | Completed with caveats | command run failed after duration; verification mismatch |
| INFO | One sentence a reader needs without DEBUG | session bookends; **command run** open/close with duration |
| DEBUG | Supports troubleshooting; safe to omit from default runs | phase transitions, `TrID transform —`, paths, flags |
| TRACE | Direct console verbose detail in CLI mode | full stderr mirror in direct mode (not file-specific) |

Do **not** emit DEBUG/TRACE content at INFO. Do **not** use INFO for progress counters when console throttling or `--trace` detail is the right tier.

## Rust / tracing (`drot`)

Use `tracing` macros with explicit targets. Audit/operator events: `target: "drot::audit"`.

`log` crate severity (lower number = more severe): Error=1, Warn=2, Info=3, Debug=4, Trace=5.

### Sink thresholds by run mode

| Run mode | Console | File (default) | File `--min` | File `--trace` |
| -------- | ------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- |
| **direct** | 5 (TRACE) | 3 (INFO) | 2 (WARN) | 4 (DEBUG) |
| **interactive** | OFF (WARN/ERROR → TUI panel) | 3 (INFO) | 2 (WARN) | 4 (DEBUG) |

## Dhara operator logs — requirements

Logs are for **humans and agents**, not aggregators. Write plain sentences, one fact per line.

### Three audit layers

| Layer | INFO | DEBUG |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| **Session bookends** | `drot started`; `drot exiting` | flags, log path, resolved paths |
| **Command run** (`CommandRun`) | `building …`; `built … in {duration}` | command args when needed |
| **Pipeline phase** | — | `phase {name} started/finished`; `TrID transform —` |

### Must do

- Wrap every command execute in `CommandRun::begin` / `complete` — always emit close INFO with duration.
- Session INFO: `drot {version} started — mode=…, workers=…` — **no log path on INFO**.
- Daily log: one `{date}_drot.log` append file + file-only `session end` record after `exiting`.
- Interactive: TUI `activity_label` + `elapsed_secs` after 4s; no INFO on console.
- Reduce stage: **no** `(N/total) reduce in progress` lines at any level.
- `--trace` reduce lines: `({current}/{total}) {file_type} — accepted|rejected: …`; stats once via `TrID transform —` at DEBUG.
- Single audit dispatch path per progress event (no duplicate callbacks).

### Must not

- Per-session numbered log files (`_N.log`).
- Phase finish or `TrID transform —` at INFO in default file runs.
- Duplicate the same stage line from runner and caller.
- Put self-referential noise on INFO (log file path, “logging initialized”).
- Log field soup / JSON blobs where one sentence suffices.

### When diagnosing

Read `{tool_root}/logs/{date}_drot.log` → `started` → `building…` / `built … in` → `exiting` → `session end` record. Use `phase ` / `TrID transform` at DEBUG for TrID depth.
